# Story sentences for the tooth chart.
# Each phrase is written with normal HumanTest steps. When the UI changes, fix it here, not in every test.

Phrase: the demo data is fresh
  Start with: fresh demo data

# ---------- opening a tooth ----------

Phrase: <user> opens tooth <n> of Ayesha
  As <user>:
    go to "/patients/a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/dental?tooth=<n>"
    "account menu" button should be visible       # the app has finished loading
    "Selected tooth" should be visible

Phrase: <user> opens tooth <n> of Karim
  As <user>:
    go to "/patients/a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002/dental?tooth=<n>"
    "account menu" button should be visible
    "Selected tooth" should be visible

# ---------- adding an issue ----------

Phrase: <user> starts adding an issue
  As <user>:
    in "Selected tooth", click "Add issue"
    "Add issue" dialog should be open

Phrase: <user> adds a "<condition>" issue with "<severity>" severity
  <user> starts adding an issue
  As <user>:
    in "Add issue" dialog, choose "<condition>" for Condition
    in "Add issue" dialog, choose "<severity>" for Severity

Phrase: <user> marks the "<surface>" surface
  As <user>:
    in "Add issue" dialog, click "<surface>"

Phrase: <user> saves the issue
  As <user>:
    in "Add issue" dialog, click "Add issue"

Phrase: the issue form should say "<message>"
  in "Add issue" dialog, should see "<message>"

# ---------- removing an issue ----------

Phrase: <user> removes the "<condition>" issue
  As <user>:
    in "Selected tooth", click "Actions for <condition>"
    click "Remove"

Phrase: <user> confirms the removal
  As <user>:
    in "Remove" dialog, click "Remove"

# ---------- what the tooth shows ----------

Phrase: tooth <n> should show "<condition>"
  in "Selected tooth", should see "<condition>"

Phrase: tooth <n> should have no active issues
  in "Selected tooth", should see "No active issues"
